@startuml c4-components
!pragma layout smetana
!include theme.iuml
title C4 Level 3: learning workspace components
rectangle "Host acceptance CLI\n[External container: Task + kubectl]\nInvokes checks against the deployed source" as Host #EEEEEE
rectangle "Learning workspace\n[Container boundary: PDE editor runtime]" {
  rectangle "Browser editor service\n[Component: code-server]\nServes course files and terminal access" as Editor
  rectangle "Notebook acceptance runner\n[Component: run-practice-labs.py]\nSelects notebooks, executes and saves evidence" as Runner
  rectangle "Module notebook kernel\n[Component: registered Jupyter kernel]\nExecutes Python or Bash exercise cells" as Kernel
  rectangle "CWL contract documentation tool\n[Component: module-specific CLI]\nValidates contracts and generates documentation" as Docs
  rectangle "Workflow execution CLI\n[Component: isolated Calrissian / cwltool]\nValidates and dispatches application execution" as CWL
  rectangle "Container execution tooling\n[Component: Podman CLI/runtime]\nBuilds and runs notebook application containers" as Podman
}
database "Workspace files\n[External data store]\nDeployed course + environments + artifacts" as Files #FFF2D5
rectangle "Kubernetes execution API\n[External platform]\nTask pod scheduling and RBAC" as API #EEEEEE
Host --> Runner : streams runner; supplies selection and kernel
Host --> Docs : invokes module's cwl:docs path
Editor --> Files : opens course and user files
Runner --> Files : reads sources; writes executed copies
Runner --> Kernel : NotebookClient starts / drives kernel
Kernel --> CWL : cells invoke workflow commands
Kernel --> Podman : cells invoke build / run commands
CWL --> API : Calrissian creates and monitors tasks
Docs --> Files : reads distributed CWL; writes docs
legend bottom
  Components are actual runtime responsibilities within one container.
  Kernel cells vary by module; they can also run Python directly or contact Dask.
  Contract-first and how-to use source task/workflow gates rather than this notebook path.
endlegend
@enduml
